ore_committed_logs\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True}],\n  \\\"description\\\":\\\"The restarted node's configuration is expected to contain itself as a voter; the defect prediction is that it does not.\\\"},\n {\\\"event\\\":\\\"restart_after_recovery\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"mode\\\",\\\"phase\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"mode_off\\\",\n  \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"after_latest_index\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":1},\n  \\\"applicability_conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"restore_committed_logs\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":False},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"snapshots\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":0}],\n  \\\"description\\\":\\\"Control: with RestoreCommittedLogs off the same restart is expected to keep the committed configuration (index 1, one voter), isolating the flagged recovery path as the cause.\\\"},\n]\ne['prefix']=e['prefix']+\\\" The harness first emits a startup_before_restart event describing the committed configuration index and server count observed before shutdown (the setup the result event depends on), then the restart_after_recovery result event; both events carry the same mode/phase identity so the two cases stay distinguishable.\\\"\njson.dump(d,open(p,'w'),indent=2)\nprint('patched')\nEOF\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-13_20-21-32-hashicorp_raft-real-run --submission update.json 2>&1 | tail -5\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
