{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_76","type":"agent_message","text":"Validation passes and the submitted harness compiles and emits the setup/result events for both modes.\n\n{\"submission\":\"update.json\",\"summary\":\"Sourced a recovery/context-validity defect in hashicorp/raft: with Config.RestoreCommittedLogs enabled, NewRaft calls restoreFromCommittedLogs (api.go:724-754), which advances lastApplied to the persisted commit index, and the startup configuration scan (api.go:610-613) then starts at max(snapshotIndex, lastApplied)+1. Committed LogConfiguration entries at or below that index are never processed (processLogs only forwards them to the FSM and never updates r.configurations), so a restarted node's membership view reverts to the snapshot's configuration or to an empty configuration when no snapshot exists. A native construction probe on a bootstrapped single node (CommitTrackingLogs, no snapshot) showed after_latest_index=0 / servers=0 / hasVote=false with the flag on versus 1/1/true with it off, and the library logged \\\"initial configuration: index=0 servers=[]\\\". A focused two-case harness (on vs off, setup event plus result event) is submitted as the fixed experiment for a retained receipt; the interpretation is scoped as conditional with the defect claim asserted, the snapshot-present variant registered as a gap, and the untested pre-runFSM processLogs blocking suspicion left outside the claim.\"}"}}
